{
 "id": 27,
 "number": 84,
 "title": "Largest Rectangle in Histogram",
 "slug": "largest-rectangle-in-histogram",
 "category": "stack",
 "difficulty": "Hard",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/largest-rectangle-in-histogram/",
 "pattern": "Monotonic increasing stack",
 "statement": "`heights[i]` is the height of a bar of width 1 in a histogram. Return the area of the largest rectangle that fits entirely inside the bars.",
 "example": {
  "input": "heights = [2,1,5,6,2,3]",
  "output": "10",
  "why": "The bars of height 5 and 6 share a rectangle of height 5 and width 2: area 10."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "heights = [2,4]",
   "output": "4"
  },
  {
   "input": "heights = [1]",
   "output": "1"
  },
  {
   "input": "heights = [2,1,2]",
   "output": "3"
  },
  {
   "input": "heights = [6,5,4,3]",
   "output": "12"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Every candidate rectangle has the full height of some bar and stretches left and right until it hits a **shorter** bar.",
  "Scan left to right with a stack of bars whose rectangle is still *open* (it has not met a shorter bar on its right yet). Their heights increase up the stack.",
  "When a shorter bar arrives, it closes every taller bar on the stack. Pop each one: its right edge is the current bar, its left edge is the bar now below it on the stack. Compute the area and keep the best."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def largestRectangleArea(self, heights: List[int]) -> int:\n        stack = []\n        max_area = 0\n\n        for i in range(len(heights)):\n            while stack and heights[i] < heights[stack[-1]]:\n                height = heights[stack.pop()]\n                width = i if not stack else i - stack[-1] - 1\n                max_area = max(max_area, height * width)\n            stack.append(i)\n\n        while stack:\n            height = heights[stack.pop()]\n            width = len(heights) if not stack else len(heights) - stack[-1] - 1\n            max_area = max(max_area, height * width)\n\n        return max_area",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n)",
  "timeWhy": "Each bar is pushed once and popped once.",
  "space": "O(n)",
  "spaceWhy": "The stack holds every bar when the heights keep increasing."
 },
